+### The deep direction: a conservative boundary representation
+
+The model's intended continuum input can be written schematically as a
+surface measure
+
+$$
+\mu_h =
+\sum_{i=1}^{N_h}
+A_i\,
+\delta_{(c_i,n_i,\ell_i,g_i)},
+$$
+
+where $A_i$ is represented area, $c_i$ centroid, $n_i$ normal,
+$\ell_i$ boundary role, and $g_i$ boundary data. The current
+industrial pipeline keeps 10,000 of approximately 17.7 million
+post-triangulation panels, each at its full-resolution tiny area. That
+is roughly 0.06% of the
+**cell indices**; the retained surface-area fraction and spatial fill
+distance have not been durably measured. It is a sparse empirical
+surface sample, not a coarse conforming discretization.
+
+A genuine coarse representation should preserve at least:
+
+$$
+\sum_i A_i \approx |\Gamma|,
+\qquad
+\sum_i A_i c_i,
+\qquad
+\sum_i A_i n_i,
+$$
+
+locally as well as globally, while retaining boundary labels, topology,
+and the trace query/source association. Its cells should cover the
+surface rather than leave almost all of it absent.
+
+The practical missed opportunity is that DrivAerML is finite. A
+multiresolution hierarchy need not be remeshed every epoch. Precompute
+5k/10k/20k/40k conservative surface levels once per car and sample
+hierarchy *levels* during training if needed.
+
+Two representation designs must not be conflated:
+
+1. A **conforming triangular coarsening/remesh** has physical vertices,
+   cells, extents, and centroids. This is the first design to test with
+   the current exact panel decoder and trace identity.
+2. A **cluster quadrature** stores representative points, areas, local
+   moments, and ancestry. It can serve a learned point/graph aggregator,
+   but it is not a triangle mesh and cannot be passed to exact panel
+   kernels without a separate element-reconstruction rule.
+
+For the first path, use topology-preserving edge collapse or remeshing
+with a conservative projection of fields and labels. For the second,
+mesh-adjacency agglomeration, geodesic Voronoi cells, or graph
+partitioning with local moment aggregation are reasonable candidates.
+Do not compare them as if they were the same intervention. The
+acceptance tests matter more than the brand:
+
+- 100% represented area up to numerical tolerance;
+- local moment conservation;
+- boundary-label purity or explicit mixed-label treatment;
+- stable normals and trace association;
+- rotation/reflection equivariance;
+- deterministic nesting across levels;
+- convergence of area-weighted fields and integrated forces after
+  projection to a common reference surface.
+
+The continuum contract also has an **output** side. Current training
+losses and field metrics reduce uniformly over retained panels. On an
+unequal-cell covering mesh, that changes the represented norm and can
+reward refinement density rather than physical area. A valid hierarchy
+therefore requires explicit target/query measures in the loss,
+validation metrics, projection, and force integration—not only source
+quadrature inside the model.
+
+Let $y^\star$ be truth on a frozen full-resolution reference surface,
+$P_h$ a restriction to representation $h$, and $R_h$ its
+prolongation. Score a coarse prediction against the unchanged truth,
+
+$$
+\lVert R_h\widehat y_h-y^\star\rVert_{L^2(\Gamma;\,A)},
+$$
+
+not against a coarse-and-reconstructed truth. Separately report the
+projection floor
+$\lVert R_hP_hy^\star-y^\star\rVert_{L^2(\Gamma;\,A)}$,
+round-trip error, scalar-integral conservation, force/moment
+conservation, and stability of tangent-vector/WSS transport when normals
+change. Otherwise projection error can masquerade as a sampler effect.
+
+The existing cluster-tree work is useful engineering prior, but its
+Morton/AABB construction is not rotation-equivariant. Reuse its batching
+and moment-aggregation ideas, not its hierarchy uncritically.
+
+This direction aligns with the modern function-space view of neural
+operators: each aggregation should be a quadrature of a defined
+continuum operator, and the output discrepancy should vanish as the
+discretization is refined. The recent
+[function-space design synthesis in *Nature Machine
+Intelligence*](https://www.nature.com/articles/s42256-026-01267-z)
+makes the same distinction between accepting variable-size arrays and
+actually defining one discretization-convergent operator.
+
+### The next experiments, in the order they should run
+
+#### Phase 0 — correctness and evidence gates, no new science run
+
+All must pass before GPU training:
+
+1. **End-to-end continuum-measure contract.** Preserve or deliberately
+   transform `MEASURE_WEIGHTS_KEY`; make every consumer's choice
+   explicit; either wire the promised total-measure scalar or remove
+   the claim. Keep physical panel extent, source quadrature measure,
+   sampling/inclusion weight, and target/query measure distinct. Test
+   geometry centering/gauging, every attention/kernel integral,
+   `LossCalculator`, `MetricCalculator`, projection, and force
+   integration on uniform and strongly nonuniform cells through the
+   public API with the actual eight-member flagship and all-boundary
+   config. The same continuum field represented on two unequal
+   refinements must give the same area-weighted objective and metric.
+2. **Audited common-surface map.** Implement the currently missing
+   projection utility; freeze and hash source/target meshes and the map.
+   Test constants, scalar integrals, projection-only and round-trip
+   error, WSS tangent transport across changed normals, and integrated
+   force/moment conservation before it is used in a model comparison.
+3. **Sampling-design fidelity.** Reproduce the production cyclic-block
+   sampler in diagnostics; inspect the actual on-disk cell order; record
+   retained area and fill distance, not only $k/N$; compare with
+   simple-random sampling before transferring any sphere-probe curve.
+   Measure the cyclic-block bias and variance of the nonlinear
+   measure-weighted RMS gauge too.
+4. **Train-only calibration.** Iterate the sampler; assert the exact set
+   of 435 case IDs equals the frozen training manifest; record the
+   manifest and split hashes; recompute $C$; and publish the change.
+5. **Resume equivalence.** Save the post-scheduler state or reorder the
+   step; add a bitwise continuous-versus-chained test including an LR
+   decay boundary.
+6. **Final checkpoint.** Always save the actual terminal state and
+   distinguish train-final from inference-checkpoint metrics.
+7. **Metric reconstruction.** Recompute current WSS tables from raw
+   predictions under both documented definitions, identify the
+   producing SHA, and retire the wrong prose.
+8. **Artifact bundle.** Recover remote configs/logs/checkpoints before
+   scratch cleanup; store hashes and label unrecoverable arms.
+9. **Barnes–Hut contract.** Add rotation tests and either fix the
+   hierarchy or state finite-$\theta$ non-equivariance.
+10. **Homogeneity domain.** Restrict the documented equation to
+    $\lambda>0$, specify and test the lower magnitude domain relative
+    to $\varepsilon$, or implement an exact nonzero branch. Do not imply
+    oddness without a separately licensed construction and test.
+
+If the historical configs and raw results cannot be recovered, say so
+once and rerun only the minimal future baseline—not the whole wave.
+
+#### Phase 1 — frozen-checkpoint compatibility screen, not a causal verdict
+
+Use frozen checkpoints to find gross incompatibilities before training,
+but respect each model's query contract.
+
+| path | valid comparison |
+|---|---|
+| Exact linear estimator | Freeze a manufactured density, kernel, and full-resolution discrete reference. At fixed queries, compare replicated cyclic-block bare/HT pairs using identical retained indices, conforming covering sources, and a simple-random diagnostic |
+| Non-trace MeshTransformer checkpoint, where available | The same source representations and 2.5k–40k counts at one fixed nested query set |
+| Trace MeshTransformer | Query $i$ must remain source cell $i$; evaluate each representation on its own aligned centroids, then use the audited map to prolong predictions to the frozen full-resolution truth surface |
+| GeoTransolver | Its surface tokens are jointly input and output; run a separate token-resolution sensitivity study, prolonging predictions to the same full-resolution truth surface rather than pretending it is a source-only factorial |
+| Geometry | Several ID cars and several already-open SHIFT development cars, not one sphere |
+
+For the fixed-query paths, the primary estimand is source representation
+at fixed source count and query set. For trace/token models, sources and
+queries still co-vary; the estimand is representation compatibility
+after projection. Repeat a predeclared, hashed set of cyclic starts
+within every car. Bare and HT variants must reuse the same retained
+indices; simple random sampling is a diagnostic, not a proxy for
+production. Report area-weighted scores against full-resolution truth,
+together with the projection floor:
+
+- signed centered field correlation;
+- positive-gain-only pattern error;
+- amplitude ratio;
+- pressure and WSS relative $L^2$;
+- integrated forces with a full-surface reference;
+- per-case failures/nonfinites;
+- wall time and memory.
+
+Include the exact linear estimator as a control. If HT weighting repairs
+that control but not the trained network, the gap could arise from
+nonlinear aggregation, learned coefficients, representation
+out-of-distribution behavior, panel-size features, trace coupling, or
+projection—not from an impossibility theorem. This control narrows the
+search; it does not uniquely localize the cause.
+
+Do **not** accept or kill the covering hypothesis from this screen.
+A checkpoint trained on cyclic-block subsampling may reject a covering mesh
+merely because the representation is out of distribution. Frozen-model
+improvement is encouraging; frozen-model degradation is inconclusive.
+
+#### Phase 2 — matched train/evaluation representation factorial
+
+Run the smallest retraining experiment that can identify adaptation to
+the substrate:
+
+| factor | levels |
+|---|---|
+| training representation | actual 10k cyclic-block sampler; 10k conforming full-cover coarsening |
+| evaluation representation | cyclic-block; covering, crossed with training representation; simple-random only as a diagnostic |
+| evaluation source count | 2.5k, 5k, 10k, 20k, and 40k for both primary representations |
+| model | minimal trace MeshTransformer and one strong token/aggregation baseline |
+| uncertainty hierarchy | paired training seeds; vehicle cases within seed; repeated predeclared cyclic-block starts within case; starts are nested observations, not independent replicates |
+| output comparison | audited prolongation of predictions to frozen full-resolution truth; area-weighted field norms, projection floor, and forces |
+
+The primary estimand is the training-representation ×
+evaluation-representation interaction, plus stability across adjacent
+covering levels. Write $t,e\in\{B,C\}$ for cyclic-block and covering
+training/evaluation representations. For paired training seed $s$,
+case $c$, and cyclic start $b$, retain the two arm contrasts
+
+$$
+L_{\mathrm{lo},t,e,s,c,b}
+  =\log\!\frac{E_{t,e,2.5k,scb}}{E_{t,e,10k,scb}},
+\qquad
+L_{\mathrm{hi},t,e,s,c,b}
+  =\log\!\frac{E_{t,e,40k,scb}}{E_{t,e,10k,scb}},
+$$
+
+The primary endpoint $E$ is area-weighted pressure relative $L^2$
+against full-resolution truth for the minimal trace MeshTransformer,
+the model in which the historical U-shape was reported. Covering
+evaluation has one deterministic value in place of $b$. Aggregate
+starts within case, then define the per-seed resolution-cliff score
+
+$$
+C_{t,e,s}
+=\operatorname{median}_{c}
+\left(
+  [\operatorname{median}_{b}L_{\mathrm{lo},t,e,s,c,b}]_+
+ +[\operatorname{median}_{b}L_{\mathrm{hi},t,e,s,c,b}]_+
+\right),
+\qquad [x]_+=\max(x,0).
+$$
+
+Never count block starts as extra cases or training seeds. The
+difference-in-differences
+
+$$
+I_s=(C_{B,C,s}-C_{B,B,s})-(C_{C,C,s}-C_{C,B,s})
+$$
+
+is the primary adaptation interaction: $I_s>0$ means matching the
+training and evaluation representation reduces the resolution cliff
+more than a main effect of either representation alone. Also report the
+same interaction separately for the low- and high-resolution arms,
+without the positive-part sum.
+
+Three paired seeds are a **variance pilot only**. Use them to choose the
+confirmatory count, then freeze the list; require at least six previously
+unused seed values, each shared across all four $t\times e$ arms, for
+a mechanism verdict. Call “most of the U-shape removed” only if:
+
+1. under cyclic training/evaluation, the seed-median of both
+   case-median contrasts exceeds $\log 2$;
+2. under covering training/evaluation, both are at most
+   $\log 1.25$;
+3. $\operatorname{median}_s\operatorname{median}_c
+   \log(\widetilde E_{C,C,10k,s,c}/
+   \widetilde E_{B,B,10k,s,c})\leq\log 1.05$, where
+   $\widetilde E$ first takes the predeclared median over block starts;
+   and
+4. both arm-specific median interactions are positive and the paired
+   $I_s$ values have the favorable sign in enough seeds for a
+   two-sided exact sign test at $\alpha=0.05$ (all six if $n=6$).
+
+Report a case-cluster bootstrap as a separate geometry-population
+sensitivity analysis; it does not replace the seed-level exact test.
+Only after the pressure/primary-model gate passes, inspect WSS, pattern,
+forces, and the baseline as prespecified ordered secondary endpoints.
+The baseline determines whether any surviving effect is
+substrate-general; it does not silently replace a failed primary
+MeshTransformer result.
+Lock these thresholds, case list, and block-start list before
+confirmatory training. Covering becomes a supported mechanism only if
+it clears that bar and improves field pattern across geometries and
+seeds. If matched retraining leaves cyclic-block and covering
+representations similar, kill covering as the dominant causal story. If
+both MeshTransformer and the baseline improve similarly, credit the
+substrate—not a MeshTransformer-specific insight.
+
+#### Phase 3 — a solver-labeled vehicle-family bridge
+
+Before another expensive RANS training wave, isolate geometry transfer
+from turbulence and label complexity. Generate high-accuracy
+panel-method potential-flow $C_p$ on conforming covering meshes, with
+mesh-convergence, residual, and reference-uncertainty checks. These are
+numerical solver labels, not exact labels.
+
+Do not build the conclusion on the 435 DrivAer training cases and the
+already-used 20-case SHIFT pilot alone. Reuse the much larger public
+car/aircraft geometry pool from M-PCNO if available, or generate
+additional parametric families; reserve family blocks rather than
+randomly mixing them. SHIFT remains development-only. Compare the
+minimal trace MeshTransformer, M-PCNO, and a strong simple baseline.
+
+The outcomes update, rather than deterministically identify, the cause:
+transfer by all methods would shift suspicion toward the RANS
+operator/labels; success only for M-PCNO would implicate the current
+architecture/representation; failure by all would argue against broad
+geometry-generalization claims and for a new data/geometry factorization.
+
+#### Phase 4 — one corrected RANS training comparison
+
+Only if Phases 2–3 support continuing:
+
+- precompute and train on a conservative 10k hierarchy level;
+- compare the minimal trace/exact-only MeshTransformer, the current
+  flagship, GeoTransolver, and M-PCNO or another
+  discretization-conscious multiscale operator;
+- report matched-parameter/matched-compute and native-capacity rows;
+- use the SHIFT pilot only for development;
+- use a seed variance pilot to choose the final seed count before the
+  untouched evaluation;
+- preserve identical data-order/subsampling seeds where pairing is
+  claimed.
+
+The industrial MeshTransformer earns another iteration only if it
+produces a spatially related field—not merely finite amplitude—and is
+competitive with the strongest baseline after its accuracy, compute,
+and parameter advantage are all stated.
+
+#### Phase 5 — one untouched geometry-family test
+
+Freeze model selection, calibration, metrics, seed count, exclusions,
+and thresholds in an externally timestamped artifact. Then evaluate
+once on:
+
+- an untouched third vehicle family, or
+- a genuinely sealed SHIFT partition whose labels have not informed
+  this program.
+
+Use hierarchical uncertainty over both cases and training seeds. Report
+absolute errors and degradation ratios. A comparator needs multiple
+seeds too; one GeoTransolver anchor is not a distribution.
+
+If the corrected MeshTransformer still has near-zero centered
+correlation or loses materially to the baseline, end the industrial
+cross-family MeshTransformer thesis. Continue the synthetic work and
+ship the industrial result as a negative study of discretization and
+geometry shift.
+
+A positive result supports transfer only to that named untouched family.
+Any broader geometry-family generalization claim requires replication on
+multiple independently held-out families.
+
+### Baselines and external positioning
+
+The nearest literature does not say “add another amplitude
+normalization.” It points toward aggregation, discretization, and
+geometry-conditioned structure.
+
+- The closest architectural overlap is
+  [Geometric Generalization of Neural Operators from a Kernel Integral
+  Perspective](https://arxiv.org/html/2602.01498). Its M-PCNO separates
+  learned singular kernel integrals into smooth Fourier far field and
+  localized near field, has $O(p^dN)$ cost (linear in point count
+  $N$ only at fixed Fourier cutoff $p$), uses
+  conventional quadrature so discretization error is tied to local mesh
+  size, and reports 8.05% mean relative error on a 500-case mixed random
+  test after training on 4,000 cases drawn from a pool of roughly 5,000
+  cars and 6,000 aircraft, each decimated to about 40,000 panels. This is
+  both a priority baseline and a novelty constraint: the multiscale
+  unknown-kernel/BIE story is already occupied. The result is not an
+  untouched cross-family test and does not settle sparse random
+  decimation or RANS, but it supplies the obvious bridge experiment and
+  makes its Ewald-style split a more relevant speed comparison than the
+  present axis-aligned Barnes--Hut backend.
+- [Principal-Part Decomposed Neural
+  Operators](https://arxiv.org/html/2606.25952) provides an even sharper
+  controlled direction. For smooth planar Laplace/Helmholtz
+  Dirichlet-to-Neumann maps, it computes a universal singular Fourier
+  multiplier exactly and learns only the smoother
+  geometry-conditioned remainder, while keeping strict linear action
+  on boundary data. Its current evidence is limited to smooth 2D
+  boundaries and moderate-frequency problems, but the decomposition is
+  a cleaner theorem-to-ablation template than claiming that two fixed
+  Laplace members carry a generic unknown nonlinear PDE.
+- [GINO](https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper_files/paper/2023/file/70518ea42831f02afc3a2828993935ad-Paper-Conference.pdf)
+  maps irregular geometry through graph neural operators to a regular
+  latent grid and explicitly targets discretization convergence. It is
+  an appropriate reference for the source-resolution experiment,
+  although its published automotive evidence is not an untouched
+  reproduction here.
+- [LinearNO](https://arxiv.org/html/2511.06294) argues that much of
+  Transolver's advantage comes from slice/deslice aggregation rather
+  than slice self-attention, reports about 40% fewer parameters and
+  36.2% less computation, and includes industrial aerodynamic tasks.
+  Whether those numbers transfer is open, but the mechanistic lesson is
+  directly relevant: simplify attention and test the aggregation.
+- [Boundary-Augmented Neural
+  Operators](https://openreview.net/pdf?id=DqZoWaDwfN) explicitly couple
+  boundary and domain representations and report robustness to
+  discretization, point distributions, and unseen geometry. It is a
+  workshop-scale result, not a settled baseline, but it is closer to the
+  program's boundary-to-interior problem statement than another
+  drive-degree arm.
+- [Geo-NeW](https://arxiv.org/html/2602.02788v2) learns
+  geometry-conditioned reduced finite-element spaces and an integral
+  balance law while enforcing conservation and boundary conditions. Its
+  evidence is currently limited to 2D steady problems and incurs an
+  implicit-solve cost, but its mesh-based ablation and unseen-geometry
+  results support testing explicit geometric/physical structure rather
+  than relying on coordinate tokens alone.
+- [Discretization mismatch in neural
+  operators](https://openreview.net/forum?id=J9FgrqOOni) shows that
+  resolution-independent parameters do not by themselves guarantee
+  consistent cross-resolution predictions. [Representation-Equivalent
+  Neural Operators](https://openreview.net/forum?id=7LSEkvEGCM)
+  formalizes the related discrete/continuous inconsistency as operator
+  aliasing. These are closer descriptions of the current failure than
+  “the operator accepts a variable number of panels.”
+- Boundary-integral positioning is already active:
+  [Learning Only On
+  Boundaries](https://arxiv.org/abs/2308.12939) trains through
+  PDE-specific boundary integral equations;
+  [Neural Green's Functions](https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.01924) learns
+  geometry-dependent solution-operator decompositions for linear PDEs;
+  and a recent [boundary-integral neural operator for mesh
+  deformation](https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.23703) learns a
+  geometry/material-aware Green traction kernel while retaining
+  linearity. These works narrow the defensible novelty here to the
+  proved angular ceiling, typed contracts, trace mechanism, and the
+  covering-versus-decimation question—not the generic idea of a learned
+  Green-like boundary kernel.
+
+These are author-reported results, not independent validations. The
+immediate recommendation is not to replace MeshTransformer wholesale.
+It is to include at least one simpler aggregation baseline and one
+discretization-conscious operator so the next experiment can distinguish
+a MeshTransformer insight from a substrate repair that helps everything.
+For the synthetic paper, PPDNO makes the highest-value comparison one of
+**licensed singular principal part versus learned smooth remainder**,
+not merely exact members versus more learned members.
+
+### Minimum result-bundle contract
+
+Every future headline row should be a directory whose identity is
+content-addressed and whose summary can be regenerated with one command.
+
+| category | required contents |
+|---|---|
+| source | commit SHA, full dirty diff, relevant-tree digest, container/lock digest |
+| configuration | resolved train and inference configs, exact commands, launch script |
+| data | manifest and case IDs, split hash, preprocessing version, units/gauge convention |
+| training | seed decomposition, effective LR history, restart history, terminal checkpoint hash/epoch |
+| evaluation | checkpoint hash, per-case metrics, raw or losslessly referenced predictions, failure/missingness rows |
+| analysis | metric definitions and code SHA, aggregation script, uncertainty method, preregistration hash |
+| performance | hardware, precision, warmups, every timing sample, memory measurement method |
+
+The synthetic `provenance.py` helper is a good start but currently
+misses nested diagnostics, the unified recipe, configs, manifests,
+launch scripts, and the environment lock. The industrial harness does
+not call it. Make the bundle creation part of the train/eval program,
+not a notebook convention.
+
