+
+These runs are completed but unharvested for ID-reference, resolution,
+and SHIFT evaluation. Their configs are not tracked, the generating
+trees have no Git identity, and the measure intervention does not
+consume incoming effective weights. The correct action is:
+
+1. archive logs, checkpoints, exact copied trees, and resolved configs;
+2. label them exploratory/non-confirmatory;
+3. investigate why the divergence guard did not stop the NaN lane;
+4. do not launch the expensive harvest as a research wave.
+
+### Two-week decision plan
+
+| window | deliverable | decision |
+|---|---|---|
+| days 1–2 | Phase-0 fixes, recovered artifact archive, corrected book status | No GPU training until complete |
+| days 3–5 | Conforming mesh pyramids on a small car subset; sampler audit and frozen compatibility screen | Authorize retraining only if the pipeline and common-surface metrics are valid |
+| day 6 | Compatibility report with raw bundle; explicitly no causal verdict yet | Freeze the minimal 2×2 retrain protocol |
+| days 7–12 | Three-paired-seed cyclic-block-versus-covering train/eval variance pilot | Estimate effect scale, sampler variance, runtime, and the confirmatory seed budget on MT and one baseline; no mechanism verdict |
+| days 13–14 | Pilot report and frozen confirmatory protocol with at least six new/common paired seeds | Kill for gross incompatibility, or authorize the confirmatory factorial—not yet the solver-labeled bridge |
+
+Subjective forecasts, stated so they can be scored:
+
+| proposition | probability |
+|---|---:|
+| The synthetic/contract paper survives a dedicated artifact audit with only scoped revisions | 75–90% |
+| Trace handling remains useful after conservative coarsening | 65–80% |
+| Conservative covering removes most of the observed resolution U-shape | 35–55% |
+| Exact singular members produce a clear industrial advantage after coverage is fixed | 10–30% |
+| Any currently trained MeshTransformer checkpoint is useful cross-family without retraining | <5% |
+| A corrected MeshTransformer beats a strong modern baseline on an untouched vehicle family | 15–35% |
+
+The key forecast is intentionally uncertain. Covering coarsening is the
+best next hypothesis because it is important and discriminable, not
+because the present evidence has already proved it.
+
+### Final assessment
+
+The program's best habit—trying to kill its own stories—eventually
+worked. It killed the fixed-gauge explanation, the seed story, the
+homogeneous-transfer story, Q2, the 41× variance story, and the premise
+that cross-family error was mostly calibration. The next act of
+discipline is to let those deaths change the queue.
+
+There are now two candidate paper directions after evidence repair:
+
+1. a controlled account of typed, contract-driven
+   boundary-to-interior operators, with exact/manufactured-label and
+   solver-verified falsification ladders; and
+2. a potentially valuable negative-to-constructive industrial study:
+   exact architectural contracts can coexist with catastrophic failure
+   under the current sparse cyclic-block sampling pipeline, while the
+   causal role of sparse support versus cell order, objective measure,
+   and representation adaptation remains to be tested. Geometry
+   generalization was not repaired by amplitude contracts alone.
+
+Trying to force both into a single triumphant MeshTransformer thesis
+will weaken them. Separating them, repairing the evidence substrate,
+and running the matched sampling-versus-coarsening experiment is the
+highest-leverage path forward.
